{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/410895-need-ideas-for-a-fae-empowered-voodoo-villain","id":410895,"title":"Need Ideas for a Fae-Empowered Voodoo Villain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-18T18:51:30-08:00","id":410895,"title":"Need Ideas for a Fae-Empowered Voodoo Villain","content":"Basically, I'm writing a little bit of fanfic, and the main villain of the piece (and if my wildest dreams come true and it evolves into an expanded universe) is a resurrected pre-Civil War plantation owner who forced a mystically inclined slave to teach him the secrets of hoodoo, in particular his signature zombification rite (which he uses to gain further control over his human property).<br /> <br /> Thing is, in this particular iteration of the nWoD, the main focus is on changelings, so his powers are themed after Contracts (and he wouldn't be caught dead allowing a Loa to ride him-he dismisses them as pagan gods of savages, they absolutely loathe him for...well, being the kind of person who calls the primary ethnicity of their faithful savages). While the Loa who grant his powers aren't True Fae in any sense changelings would recognize, they are forced to serve as his power source by dint of ancient oaths that gurantee fair granting of powers, even to <i>bokors </i>that make other <i>bokors </i>look like saints. I actually plan on him being defeated when he is tricked into breaking the terms of the oath, allowing the Loa to exact long overdo justice, but I digress.<br /> <br /> So apart from the zombification abilities, what kind of Fae and Contract-themed powers would you see a <i>bokor </i>who doesn't actually care about the religion in any meaningful way having?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T19:17:26-08:00","id":410924,"title":"","content":"Have you ever watched Disney's The Princess and the Frog? While Dr. Facilier appears rather different than what your guy sounds like, he does have a few tricks. One is a &quot;Token&quot; that allows you to appear like another person, though its &quot;Catch&quot; requires it to regularly take a sample of the victim's blood. He's also able to create a variety of illusions using special powder(though I know little of the occult, I believe the real life term is &quot;gris-gris&quot;, or something of that sort), and he has a number of shadowy, demonic spirits under his control, including one that appears to have replaced his own shadow. <br /> <br /> There's also always the classic Voodoo doll, of course.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, in regards to Facilier, you know how you wanted your bad guy to go? Search Youtube for &quot;Friends on the Other Side(Reprise)&quot;. You won't be disapointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Thought of something 02-18-2015, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T21:29:35-08:00","id":411019,"title":"","content":"Do you want this to be representative of actual Voodoo or Vodoun, or based on the Hollywood conception of zombies and magic dolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:48:32-08:00","id":411107,"title":"","content":"When you say you want &quot;Fae and Contract-themed powers&quot; do you mean you want to know what Contracts can do voodooish things or are you looking for custom voodoosih powers that have a fairy flair to them?<br /> <br /> If you're looking for the former the first thing the springs to mind is that Contracts of Communion: Flesh is a totally valid way to raise a zombie. If it's the later I'd recommend voodoo doll/curse like powers that can only be used on those he has a Pledge with, maybe as a unique Pledge Boon/Task for himself/his victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:14:48-08:00","id":411323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/410895-need-ideas-for-a-fae-empowered-voodoo-villain?p=411019#post411019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want this to be representative of actual Voodoo or Vodoun, or based on the Hollywood conception of zombies and magic dolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, deliberately Hollywood-ish, again this isn't a believer in the religion, just someone who uses it to gain more power-it's slapdash and lacking in any actual reverence. The exception are the zombis, who are generally living people with their souls removed to make them compliant and largely mindless slaves. I'm drawing on Hati's view of zombi as menial labourer here.<br /> <br /> @helel: Little of column A, little of Column B. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T11:12:23-08:00","id":411808,"title":"","content":"Contracts of Communion and Contracts of Elements can both get some very nice and visceral effects with the elements Blood, Bone, and Flesh. Communion will let you raise &quot;zombies&quot; and &quot;skeletons&quot; while Elements Blood can let you choke someone on their own blood once you've cut them to let some of it out. I would caution for balance sake you only let these Contracts effect the body once it's detached or dead. No taking control of the blood inside someone's brain to give them a stroke. Finally Contracts of Spell-bound Autumn are generally good as a &quot;master of magic&quot; type thing and lets him talk with loa.<br /> <br /> This character could have a Token voodoo doll that lets him cast Contracts it to have them effect those he has pledges with no matter where they be. That would cover your classic Voodoo doll trope. Catch could be that you have some of the targets hair or blood to fuel it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:26:35-08:00","id":411998,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m curious about the cost of the Contracts, if lacking glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:03:37-08:00","id":412133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/410895-need-ideas-for-a-fae-empowered-voodoo-villain?p=411998#post411998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u00b4m curious about the cost of the Contracts, if lacking glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Good point.<br /> <br /> I was thinking he has a mojo bag to help him, and you just thought of a reason he has it-it allows him to gather Glamour and store it like a changeling. Otherwise it's all chanting and Pledges. <br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:15:54-08:00","id":412144,"title":"","content":"How about making it all Pledge based? At least in the basic concept: zombi are humans who are bound by ridiculously unfair and accidental oaths: feel no pain and get a bit stronger but at the cost of being bound to the bokor's commands, to the degree of appearing mindless.<br /> <br /> The Loa (aka. The Wyrd) just can't wait for this guy to fail the conditions on his side of the pledge. The punishment he'd be due would chill the blood...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T15:55:49-08:00","id":412170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about making it all Pledge based? At least in the basic concept: zombi are humans who are bound by ridiculously unfair and accidental oaths: feel no pain and get a bit stronger but at the cost of being bound to the bokor's commands, to the degree of appearing mindless. </div> </div> </div>So, using the system for Pledges and Goblin Vows? It could work, specially if the villain doesn\u00b4t know the price he must pay each time he summons the Loa\u00b4s power (maybe the chanting is not in English).<br /> <br /> Update: maybe one of the tokens he stole acts as a credit card, allowing him to buy more than he should and delaying the moment of payment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 02-20-2015, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:31:17-08:00","id":417515,"title":"","content":"Simple solution to the zombii question: Give him knowledge of that alleged &quot;zombie potion&quot; they supposedly use in Haiti (the one that includes blowfish poison). Turns out if you mix it together and let it sit in the hedge it becomes a one use token that allows you to capture the soul of those who drink it. Use the Thrall stats from Goblin Markets for the leftover body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}